Your REPL should simply dispatch the line:
public void runRepl() {
    Scanner scan = new Scanner(System.in);

    while (true) {
        System.out.print(COMMAND_PROMPT);

        if (!scan.hasNextLine()) {
            break;
        }

        String command = scan.nextLine().trim();

        if (command.equals("exit")) {
            break;
        }

        try {
            processInput(command);
        } catch (Exception e) {
            System.err.println(e.getMessage());
        }
    }

    scan.close();
}

This also avoids throwing an exception when stdin reaches EOF.

One important issue with buildForkedShell()
Your implementation is close, but there's a subtle parsing issue.
Currently:
int redirectIndex = actualCommand.indexOf(">");

will accept something like:
